{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1471242-aberrant-quantum-tech-mjolnir","id":1471242,"title":"Aberrant quantum tech mjolnir","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-25T12:24:59-08:00","id":1471242,"title":"Aberrant quantum tech mjolnir","content":"I'm curious how you would go about making mjolnir as quantum tech. What would you rank it as and how would you stat it up?<br /> <br /> I'm also a bit curious about how you can use quantum tech to enhance a novas existing powers for example a nova with weather related powers using a q-tech device to enhance his abilities rather than give him new ones. The rules in the book don't really cover it that well and seem really lacklustre.<br /> <br /> In my head I'm imagining a nova with powers like Thor and having a quantum tech version of mjolnir to enhance his abilities to maybe greater scale or have enhancement to his rolls etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-25T15:58:08-08:00","id":1471251,"title":"","content":"Is there a workaround for making a device that has a narrative ability, like how Captain America's shield is Unbreakable or how Mjolnir is Unmovable? The effect might end up being more cosmetic than anything, though. Just from a game balance perspective. Like Captain America's shield is Unbreakable but someone using it wouldn't be 100 percent bulletproof. They could still get shot in the legs. So, in a game system perspective Captain America's shield wouldn't normally be able to be broken (unless you get to very high Scale) but it would still only give an enhancement bonus to the person using it rather than immunity to damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-25T18:06:15-08:00","id":1471256,"title":"","content":"These are great ideas!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T14:13:34-08:00","id":1471300,"title":"","content":"Two Options come to mind:<br /> <br /> Nr. 1: Just tag on the abilities that you want to boost and call it a day.<br /> <br /> Nr. 2: Tag on the abilities that you want to boost AND tag on the needed Quantum on top of that... cause Mjolnir in this case acts as a Booster Artifact.<br /> Point in Case -&gt; Jane, who gets to wear the mantle in the comics and is just a mortal but not with the hammer just because she's worthy.<br /> Another point in case -&gt; Thor was definitely weaker (less Quantum, less access to powers/Mega-stuff, while depowered by Odin... although his power didn't really come from the hammer, despite his belief), Mjolnir was more a crutch for him<br /> <br /> Personally? I'd prefer that solution. I've no time right now to have a look at how it should be priced... and to be honest I haven't tinkered all that much with Super Science stuff, since my group isn't up to the gills there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1471242-aberrant-quantum-tech-mjolnir?p=1471251#post1471251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a workaround for making a device that has a narrative ability, like how Captain America's shield is Unbreakable or how Mjolnir is Unmovable? The effect might end up being more cosmetic than anything, though. Just from a game balance perspective. Like Captain America's shield is Unbreakable but someone using it wouldn't be 100 percent bulletproof. They could still get shot in the legs. So, in a game system perspective Captain America's shield wouldn't normally be able to be broken (unless you get to very high Scale) but it would still only give an enhancement bonus to the person using it rather than immunity to damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's just cosmetic I wouldn't worry to much. Either wing it or discuss at your table. As long as nobody get's effed over - and even that can be fun if the player(s) get a headsup - then all should be good. It's like handing out a trait that let's nobody age anymore. Whoop-deee-dooo... cool on paper, usually pointless to nick points from a player for that cause it's usually rather irrelevant.<br /> And in any campaign where it is relevant? It's a narrative baseline anyway.<br /> <br /> If your table is game? Get yourself an unbreakable shield or some unmoveable weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","name":"Bhurano","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T17:55:04-08:00","id":1471308,"title":"","content":"I think the 'Loyal to a Fault' crafting Flaw could offer a partial explanation for why only Thor can wield Mjolnir. You could also use a variant of the Massive vehicle tag to up the durability &amp; weight without actually upping the size. You could do something similar to explain why Captain America's shield is virtually impervious to damage; it has a high durability scale combined with Absorption (kinetic energy).<br /> <br /> Since nova Super-Science can grant quantum traits, you could technically imbue Mjolnir with the Technique Mega-Edge so it provides Thor with a new ability derived from an ability he already has. If a new wielder lacks that prerequisite ability, they can't use Mjolnir to manifest the variant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T18:15:32-08:00","id":1471310,"title":"","content":"Mjolnir is not heavy, it\u2019s loyal, so using rules to increase its weight is not the best option. The point is, you can\u2019t use Mjolnir, and using it is basically lift it and let it fall, so you can\u2019t even lift it.<br /> <br /> You could have a Loyal to a Rule as a flaw, that would leave even Thor out of the list of possible users until he is worth again.<br /> <br /> Now, Cap Shield is another thing. A Shield has the Shield tag (I thing it\u2019s from Scion) that adds 2 to defense when used to defense). A regular shield would not block high scale attacks, basically it would be useless against a bazooka or a car being thrown in the user, but Caps Shield is still useful against high scale attacks (to a certain point, something like scale 5 attack or so).<br /> <br /> That is basically how I would rule each of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T18:51:53-08:00","id":1471312,"title":"","content":"Captain America's Shield being partially modeled by ignoring Scale difference seems appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T19:13:50-08:00","id":1471313,"title":"","content":"Captain America shield, you could give it absorption for kinetic energy maybe. So something like high scale durability plus absorption, not sure what else maybe some sort of ability that lets you throw it and summon it back.<br /> <br /> Another idea I had for quantum tech if your a nova in the aeon setting on earth is a watch which hides you from been detected by tech or psions psiads etc without having to dorm down and be left vulnerable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T20:39:50-08:00","id":1471314,"title":"","content":"Cap's shield has Durability Scale. It also has Flight with a highly limited use of &quot;Returns to the thrower&quot; so it would be extremely cheap and allows you to throw some other tags in there as well.<br /> With something like Mjolnir, you could make a custom Tag of &quot;Only works for those are worthy&quot; and then work out with the SG what &quot;worthy&quot; means and go from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T03:20:49-08:00","id":1471321,"title":"","content":"Wouldn\u2019t it work if you used Quantum Deflection with Reduced Cost 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}